---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — F1 Delta"
  description="Privacy Policy for F1 Delta (f1delta.com) — how we collect, use, and protect information."
  canonical="https://f1delta.com/privacy-policy"
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: 7 July 2026</p>

    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how F1 Delta ("F1 Delta," "we," "us," or "the site"), operated by an individual based in Michigan, United States, collects, uses, and protects information when you visit f1delta.com.</p>
    <p>By using the site, you agree to the practices described here. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>F1 Delta is an independent, individually operated Formula 1 reference website. For any privacy questions, contact <a href="mailto:f1deltasupport@gmail.com">f1deltasupport@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    <p>For visitors in the European Economic Area (EEA) and the United Kingdom, the site operator acts as the data controller for personal data processed through f1delta.com.</p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>Information you provide.</strong> F1 Delta has no account system and doesn't require you to submit personal information to browse. If you email us or make a payment to remove ads, we receive the information you provide (such as your email address and, for payments, details handled by our payment processor).</p>
    <p><strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> Like most websites, we and our service providers automatically collect certain technical information when you visit, which may include your IP address, browser type, device type, operating system, referring pages, pages viewed, and general usage patterns. This is collected through cookies and similar technologies (see below).</p>

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small files stored on your device. F1 Delta and its partners use them for:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Analytics</strong> — to understand how visitors use the site so we can improve it (via Google Analytics).</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising</strong> — to display ads and, where you consent, to make them more relevant (via Google AdSense).</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Google AdSense.</strong> We use Google AdSense to display advertisements. Google and third-party vendors use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites. You can learn how Google uses information from sites that use its services at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>, and you can opt out of personalized advertising via <a href="https://adssettings.google.com">Google Ads Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices">aboutads.info/choices</a>.</p>
    <p><strong>Google Analytics.</strong> We use Google Analytics (GA4) to measure traffic and usage. Google Analytics sets cookies to help analyze how visitors use the site. Learn more at <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Consent (EEA and UK)</h2>
    <p>If you're visiting from the EEA or the UK, we present a consent banner when you arrive. We rely on your consent as the legal basis for advertising and analytics cookies, and we don't set non-essential cookies until you provide it. You can withdraw or change your consent at any time via the consent controls on the site.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights over your personal data:</p>
    <p><strong>EEA / UK (GDPR).</strong> You have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict, or object to the processing of your personal data, the right to data portability, and the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.</p>
    <p><strong>California (CCPA/CPRA).</strong> You have the right to know what personal information is collected, to request its deletion, and to opt out of the "sale" or "sharing" of personal information. F1 Delta does not sell your personal information for money.</p>
    <p>To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:f1deltasupport@gmail.com">f1deltasupport@gmail.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>F1 Delta relies on third-party providers that may process limited data on our behalf or under their own policies:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google AdSense</strong> — advertising (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — analytics (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — content delivery and security (<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>Netlify</strong> — website hosting (<a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/">privacy policy</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — payment processing for ad removal (<a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>Ko-fi</strong> — donations, handled on Ko-fi's own platform (<a href="https://more.ko-fi.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't control these providers' own data practices; please review their policies.</p>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>F1 Delta is not directed at children under 13 (or the minimum age required in your jurisdiction), and we don't knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>

    <h2>Data retention and security</h2>
    <p>We keep personal data only as long as needed for the purposes described here, and we take reasonable measures to protect it. No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, however, and we can't guarantee absolute security.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by the "Last updated" date above. Continued use of the site after changes means you accept the revised policy.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy or your data: <a href="mailto:f1deltasupport@gmail.com">f1deltasupport@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

